    "content": "This document outlines coding standards for software development at Nexora Technologies Pvt. Ltd., particularly for backend development activities. It includes:\n\n1. **Functions and Classes**:\n   - Functions defined include `calculateSalary()`, `sendInvoiceEmail()`, and `validateUser()` which are likely part of a service.\n   - There is also an `EmployeeService` class, an `AuthenticationManager` class, and constants such as `MAX_LOGIN_ATTEMPTS`, `DEFAULT_TIMEOUT`, and `API_VERSION`.\n\n2. **File Organization**:\n   - The document recommends organizing code into structured directories like `controllers/`, `services/`, `models/`, `repositories/`, `middlewares/`, `utilities/`, `config/`, and `tests/`.\n   - Each file should have a clear responsibility to avoid redundancy.\n   - Code files should not exceed 500 lines for maintainability.\n\n3. **Coding Standards**:\n   - Developers are instructed to write unit tests, integration tests, and API tests with at least an 80% code coverage target.\n   - The document recommends minimizing database queries, caching frequently accessed data, removing duplicate code, and optimizing API responses for performance improvement.\n   - Third-party libraries need verification regarding licensing and maintenance status before inclusion.\n\n4. **Formatting Standards**:\n   - Code should use a 4-space indentation with UTF-8 encoding and Unix (LF) line endings.\n   - The maximum length of each line is 120 characters, ensuring readability.\n   - Indentation must be consistent; one statement per line is encouraged.\n   - Trailing whitespace should be removed.\n\n5. **Documentation**:\n   - Documentation is essential for major features and includes explanations of purpose, configuration, dependencies, architecture overview, and deployment notes.\n\n6. **Error Handling**:\n   - Error handling comments explain the rationale behind error processing rather than describing what specific operations an application does.\n   \nThis document provides a comprehensive framework to ensure high-quality, maintainable, secure, readable, and collaborative software development practices at Nexora Technologies Pvt. Ltd.",
